auth {
  mode: none
}

headers {
  x-user-email: {{ownerEmail}}
}

docs {
  # vinylTrack API

  Exercises the API over HTTP against a running stack — the thing the
  in-process supertest suite structurally cannot do (it imports `app.ts`
  directly and never boots a listener).

  ## Running

  Start the stack and seed it, then:

      docker compose up -d
      docker compose run --rm seed
      cd be && npm run test:api

  Or open this folder in the Bruno app and pick the `local` environment.

  ## Identities

  Caller identity is the `x-user-email` dev header (#26), defaulted here at
  the collection level and overridden per request. The seeded users are:

  | var             | user                | access                          |
  |-----------------|---------------------|---------------------------------|
  | `ownerEmail`    | kevin@example.com   | admin; owns both collections    |
  | `sharedEmail`   | alex@example.com    | shared on Vinyl only            |
  | `outsiderEmail` | jamie@example.com   | owns nothing, shared nothing    |
  | `unknownEmail`  | nobody@example.com  | not a user at all — expects 401 |

  `ownerEmail` is *also* the admin, so admin-gated requests use it too;
  non-admin negative cases use `sharedEmail`.

  ## Ordering

  Requests run in `seq` order and chain ids through runtime vars, so the
  folders are ordered by dependency: collection -> artist -> location ->
  album -> copy -> want -> cleanup. The `cleanup` folder removes everything
  the run created, so repeated runs stay idempotent.
}
